<title>SINGAPORE: Acer raises stake in African subsidiary.</title>
<headline>Acer raises stake in African subsidiary.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Acer Computer International Ltd (ACI) said in a statement on Thursday it had increased its stakes in Acer Africa (Proprietary) Ltd on August 26.</p>
<p>The statement said the increase was raised through ACI making capital loans amounting to 16.8 million rand (US$3.7 million) to Acer Africa between 1994 and 1995.</p>
<p>It said ACI now owned 34.3 million shares, or 93.2 percent, from 17.5 million shares previously.</p>
<p>The remaining shares are held in a trust for Acer Africa employees.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
